{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZXfP2986RPcz1EajRS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The batch is reviewed and saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. Validation with `--batch A05,A06,A07,C01,C02 --before-challenges` printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.` I did not run challenges, and nothing was run or networked.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 | gap | Nothing resolves the type ID (`identity.py:75`) to a stored manifest or live instance. Ownership is a team name only, with no operator or on-call. The only stop control is a fleet or tenant halt (`killswitch.py:19`). |\n| A06 | gap | `child()` gives the extractor a new instance ID and a parent link, but it copies the parent's type ID (`identity.py:51`). Prompt capture is set to `false` (`deployment.yaml:67`). No approved audit role is set up for stored prompt text. |\n| A07 | gap | Both models are listed and pinned. Their configuration is not recorded per model. Extractor outcomes carry no model ID (`extractor.py:87`). The served model is logged but never compared with the expected one (`extractor.py:80`). |\n| C01 | gap | The model records, pinned-snapshot labels and \"not applicable\" training are fine. Network and image policy have no version, digest or owner (`manifest.yaml:34-35`). Permission scopes, budgets and the MCP and issuer bindings are not listed. |\n| C02 | gap | There is no CODEOWNERS or review rule in the repo. The release job has no protected environment (`ci.yaml:40`). The emergency path is rated unknown, since the repo has no emergency-change procedure and the only pointer is to an outside runbook. |\n\nFive checks are `yes`: A06.2, A07.1, C01.2, C01.3 and C01.5. A06.2 and A07.1 are `yes` because the extractor is the only spawn path and the only helper model. They each have a coverage ledger.\n\n- **Prescan hits:** the seven hits (H001–H007) belong to B07, B08, B09, B11 and R05, so I left them unresolved. The scope text says so.\n- **Items not run:** the item-level checks I deliberately did not run are the challenges, so no `likely_pass` ratings exist yet.\n- **Files added:** the coverage and attempt files are in `work/`. The prescan and inventory output is in `agent/` (`brace-prescan.json`, `brace-inventory.json`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":90870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":618},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a772fce6-3235-4ab2-ba24-c62b009a560f","uuid":"672e88b7-5d20-4e8b-91a7-72dcd9775e2a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:23:42.138Z","request_id":"req_011CgDZXf5vMSKqEHLMsCUdN"}
